LeetCode 410 – Split Array Largest Sum

This problem challenged me to think beyond a normal Binary Search. I learned how Binary Search on the Answer combined with a Greedy Validation approach can solve optimization problems efficiently.

💡 Approach: Binary Search + Greedy Validation (O(n log(sum)))

Instead of checking every possible way to split the array, I performed Binary Search on the range of possible answers (maximum subarray sum). For every candidate value, I used a greedy validation function to determine whether the array could be divided into k subarrays while keeping each subarray sum within the given limit. Based on the result, I narrowed down the search space until I found the minimum possible largest sum.

📚 Key Learnings:
✅ Understanding the Binary Search on Answer technique
✅ Combining Binary Search with a Greedy validation function
✅ Solving optimization problems efficiently
✅ Reducing the brute-force approach to O(n log(sum))
✅ Strengthening problem-solving skills for Hard-level questions

